{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Copying source.img to a chosen destination preserves its 67,108,864-byte logical length and exact contents while allocating less than 2 MiB.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The destination matched source.img by cmp and SHA-256, retained the 64 MiB logical size, and used only 20,480 allocated bytes. The same properties remained after restart and another copy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9c54b6dec9a54133","cmd-405a9c483f204daf"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"source.img remains intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The source retained its prepared-state SHA-256, size, sparse allocation, and inode. A same-file copy was rejected without changing its hash or inode.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-8f2bf9e5f7ed4dbd","cmd-2a09c80844c546a5","cmd-405a9c483f204daf"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Repeated copying to the same destination is safe.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A repeated copy completed successfully through replacement of the destination, remained byte-identical and sparse, and left no utility temporary directories. Recopying also succeeded after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d127d8bc153a4be4","cmd-405a9c483f204daf"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"The repaired utility works on the legacy platform without changing the installed operating-system release or kernel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repair is executable and valid under /bin/sh, uses the installed GNU coreutils 5.97 sparse-copy capability, and demonstrably performs the required copy. CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were unchanged after execution and restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7296fe51867648b9","cmd-eb88e6b531f146fa","cmd-9c54b6dec9a54133","cmd-405a9c483f204daf","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"The state-changing actions were causally connected to installing the repair, producing and testing the requested destination, establishing repeat safety, or completing the mandatory restart protocol. The failed unprivileged edit did not change the utility. No unrelated managed-state mutation is evidenced. One temporary acknowledgement file created during restart evidence collection remained at /tmp/antrieb-reboot-ack; its creation supported the restart protocol, but retaining it was unnecessary residue and it was not reverted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0f8128e278ed44a0","cmd-e5f76252157e4a2d","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide node-restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot ID corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered SSH, utility, source data, sparse destination, and repeat-copy behavior.","limitations":["System-wide hygiene coverage is incomplete because failed-service collection was unsupported on this CentOS release and the lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum operation; neither observation shows executor-caused damage.","The retained /tmp/antrieb-reboot-ack file is minor executor-created residue."]}
